# Cache policy for the deployed app.
#
# Flutter web does not content-hash its output: every build emits the same
# main.dart.js / flutter_bootstrap.js / index.html names. A normal max-age
# would therefore serve a stale app after a deploy until the TTL expired.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "do not store" - the browser still keeps the file
# but must revalidate it against the edge before reusing it. Cloudflare answers
# with a 304 (a few hundred bytes) when nothing changed, so repeat loads stay
# fast, and a deploy is picked up on the very next request. No manual cache
# clearing, ever.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
